A||||9||mbramble||El Cheapo "Paint Job"||||1||
Z||000000||mbramble||04-29-2000||09:11 PM||||I inherited my '87 coupe from my son when he went in the Navy and decided it wasn't reliable enough to take across country. He in turn had bought it from his sister after she got married and moved away.  It has been in the family for about 5 years.  With help from this forum, I was able to have the 4 banger repaired (bad coil pack) and it is now VERY reliable. <P>When I got it, the paint on the roof, trunk lid and clip was orange peeled, faded and flaking off.  I had sanded it and primed it and was hoping to get it painted at some time.  Estimates ranged from $300-500 for just an average paint job -- nothing special.  Though I have the money to have it painted, I felt I could spend it better on other things first.  But, the terrible looks of the car left me less than inspired to do other things to improve the looks.  Another son was down from NY this past week and he dabbles in body work.  We went out and bought a can of PlastiCoat paint that matched the factory color and worked on one rear fender.  It came out beautiful!  So, I went and bought 10 more cans and some clear coat and we painted all the areas that were primered.  Now, I need to do some more sanding on the clear coat but it really looks nice.  It is especially nice in one of the areas where there was a drip and we sanded extra there.  That section looks just as good as the front of the car.  We just ran out of time but I will get back to sanding next weekend. <BR>We put on a very thin coat of paint, a much thicker coat and sanded with 2000 grit paper.  Then another coat, another sanding and then some polishing compound. Then two coats of clearcoat and sanding.  Then we applied a scatch remover and then a glaze.  There are some streaks on the deck lid but I think additional sanding will take them out.  If this only lasts a year, I will be more than happy.  I spent about $50 and probably 10 hours apiece in labor -- with more sanding to follow.  The car really looks great -- not showroom quality by any stretch but it ain't a showroom car!!  It's a daily driver that I really love to drive.<BR>I am one happy camper!!!  Oh yea, this was all inspired by someone on the Forum who started working on his front facia and posed the question could he paint his whole car with spraycans.  I have long been 'afraid' to tackle painting but after this very successful experience, I will buy a spraygun and auto paint the next time I need to paint the car and do it myself using my compressor. <P>Sorry for being so long winded but I really feel good about my car today!!!<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||04-29-2000||09:21 PM||||If you like it Mike, We love it!!!<P>It's all part of this  Fiero game that we play  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The never ending game!!<BR>You up to doing a little upholstery<BR>work next?||||reg||1
Z||000002||mbramble||04-29-2000||11:13 PM||||Actually, next I'm gona rip out the entire center console and replace the plastic 'rail' that everything is attached to.  All the screw holesa re stripped out in mine so I can't tighten the components down securely.  And, using info found on the Forum, I am going to repair the console sections where the vinyl/padding has separated from the frame.  Then, I'm gonna replace the headliner -- after experimenting with the one on my S-10!!  And replace the rear speakers at the same time.....<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||04-30-2000||11:26 AM||||Have to admit that I've done that too. One of the auto parts stores in my area actually will mix cans of base/clear that I've used and had good results with. They custom mix a standard size spray can with fan spray valve for $5.20 each. <P>Taking the time to color sand afterward will make all the difference.||||reg||1
Z||000004||CUTTER||05-01-2000||01:38 AM||||Mbramble, that was me that posted that topic about painting my front facia, spoiler and ground effects. It does look good! Im glad I posted that topic because I was able to convince a fellow fieroer that it does look good and you tried it and agree. I feel pretty good now!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>    CUTTER blue87GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||mbramble||05-01-2000||10:13 AM||||Thanks Cutter, for the inspiration.  Just can't say enough about how nice it is to look out the window at a fully painted car and know it cost me $50 in paint/clearcoat!!!  ||||reg||1
