Z||000007||batboy||05-02-2000||03:45 PM||||Those that have looked at my website and saw the pics of my baby blue 1936 Ford truck were looking at a spray can paint job too. It's an old farm truck with lots of little dings and dents, but nearly no rust, so I bombed it until I could find new fenders and could afford to have the cab worked on. I've had several people that wouldn't believe it was a spray can job. Mask off everything well, be careful, and take your time, it's better than nothing!||||reg||1
Z||000008||deceler8||05-04-2000||06:07 PM||||Just in the last two days I sanded down my pitiful faded decklid and resprayed it with clear coat in a can...I'm amazed at how good it looks. Shines just like a new car.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mbramble||05-23-2000||06:25 PM||||Finally got a couple of photos:<P>The top and front pillars, deck lid and upper rear fender sections were painted.  By the way, I do have some turbo wheels that I am currently stripping/polishing to put on later....<BR> <A HREF="http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/car1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/car1.jpg</A>  <A HREF="http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/car2.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.bramblett.com/fiero/car2.jpg</A> ||||reg||1
